RF.put("questb:b66",{"8706":{"id":8706,"t":"Hammer of the Gathering Storm","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 1 Qiraji Spiked Hilt, 2 Amber Idols, 5 Ivory Scarabs and 5 Bronze Scarabs to Warden Haro in Silithus. You must also attain Exalted reputation with Cenarion Circle to complete this quest.\nQiraji Spiked Hilt Ossirian the Unscarred 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Moam 40 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Ayamiss the Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Buru the Gorger 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj\n2 Amber Idol Flesh Hunter 10 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Drone 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Collector 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Hive'Zara Soldier 0.5 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj and 4 more\n5 Bronze Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Ivory Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 42000 reputation with Cenarion Circle","desc":"The Qiraji and their servants wield items made with the rarest and finest materials: bones from gargantuan ancient creatures, gems from the depths of the earth, metals pure and strong.\nJust the sight of Qiraji artifacts fills me with an urge to practice my craft with their shattered and smelted pieces. Prove your allegiance to the Circle, ‹name›, and I will make you a powerful weapon from the finest Qiraji materials.","rew":"You will receive:\nHammer of the Gathering Storm\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Did you bring me the components I require, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹class›. This is a masterwork hilt... the balance is perfect.\nTake your weapon, ‹name›. Wield it with great confidence and vanquish our enemies!","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.1,"y":38.9,"n":"Warden Haro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8626":{"id":8626,"t":"Striker's Footguards","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,950, 0.66 times as much.","obj":"Bring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj. This quest also requires Neutral faction with the Brood of Nozdormu.\nQiraji Bindings of Command Viscidus in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Princess Huhuran in Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n2 Idol of Life Vekniss Soldier 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Stinger 0.5 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Stone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\n5 Bone Scarab Flesh Hunter 1 % in Ruins of Ahn'Qiraj , Vekniss Soldier 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Warrior 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple , Vekniss Guardian 1 % in Ahn'Qiraj Temple and 4 more\nReach 0 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","desc":"Qiraji magic is strong and ancient. The most powerful qiraji wield items of such might, they'd give pause even to a dragon.\nBring me the qiraji bindings of command and other minor components by and I'll create a set of powerful boots for you.\nYou will find them useful in the fight against the enemy.","rew":"You will receive:\nStriker's Footguards\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Brood of Nozdormu","back":"You've acquired the items I requested, ‹name›?","done":"You've done well, ‹name›. You've proven you're no ordinary mortal.\nI give you these with the confidence they'll aid you in crushing the vile qiraji.\nStart Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple End Kandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple Level 60 , requires level 60 Difficulty 60 Side Both factions Class Hunter Type Raid Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 8626\nThe chain\n2 quests at level 60, 13,200 XP in all.\n1 [ 60 ] Mortal Champions\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP\n2 [ 60 ] Striker's Footguards this quest\nBring the Qiraji Bindings of Command, 2 Idols of Life, 5 Stone Scarabs and 5 Bone Scarabs to Kandrostrasz in Ahn'Qiraj.\nKandrostrasz Ahn'Qiraj Temple\n6,600 XP","cats":["ahnqiraj"]},"8546":{"id":8546,"t":"The Horde Needs More Mithril Bars!","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 20 Mithril Bars to Senior Sergeant T'kelah at the Valley of Spirits in Orgrimmar.\n20 Mithril Bar","desc":"Yup, I be glad you're here, mon. You helped me before, and now I need your help again. We still lookin' ta bring in more mithril bars for the war effort; gonna build lots of armor and weapons and things to go squish them bugs at Ahn'Qiraj.\nSo if you be a true friend, you bring me back more stacks of mithril bars. I take all you got until we hit our quota. You have some for me now?","rew":"You will receive:\n7 Horde Commendation Signet Ahn'Qiraj War Effort Supplies","done":"That be good work ‹name›! Another twenty bars get us that much closer to the goal, and get us more war materiel. I see to it they get put away. And if you get another stack of mithril bars mon, you make sure to be bringin' them here to me.","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":31.3,"y":66.1,"n":"Senior Sergeant T'kelah","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ahnqiraj-war"]},"7026":{"id":7026,"t":"Ram Riding Harnesses","lv":60,"min":51,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"null\nFrostwolf Hide Frostwolf 80 % in Alterac Valley , Stabled Frostwolf 80 % in Alterac Valley , Frostwolf Bloodhound 80 % in Alterac Valley","desc":"The Stormpike Brigade cannot charge into battle bareback! We require harnesses for our mounts, after all, we are not savages.\nWhile we could easily slay the rams that roam near our base for the leather required to fashion a harness, doing so would be idiotic. We need those rams for mounts.\nYou must strike at our enemy's base, slaying the frostwolves they use as mounts and taking their hides. Return their hides to me so that harnesses may be made for the cavalry. Go!","back":"Slaying the frostwolves they use as mounts and return their hides to me.","done":"Well done, soldier. I will notify you when I have stockpiled enough of the hides.\nCarry on!\nStart Stormpike Ram Rider Commander Alterac Valley End Stormpike Ram Rider Commander Alterac Valley Level 60 , requires level 51 Difficulty 51 56 58 Side Alliance Type PvP Shareable Yes Repeatable Yes Quest ID 7026","cats":["alterac-valley"]},"6546":{"id":6546,"t":"Warsong Outrider Update","lv":25,"min":17,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Warsong Report","rew":"You will receive:\nWarsong Outrider Update","back":"Much danger lies along this path, ‹name›. You'd do best to remember this while traveling in these lands. The threat of the alliance is quite near.\nWe are faced by enemies on all fronts. The satyr are a formidable and prevalent force in eastern Ashenvale. I have also discovered that the naga have taken over a large area of the land of Azshara.\nIt's good to see that we are still bolstering our numbers -- be ready for what lies ahead, ‹name›.","done":"Take my update to Kadrak. Swiftly, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":81.8,"y":53.5,"n":"Warsong Outrider","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"1026":{"id":1026,"t":"Raene's Cleansing","lv":27,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find the Wooden Key and a piece of Dartol's Rod before returning to Shael'dryn at the moonwell.\nIron Shaft Worn Chest","desc":"I wish your tidings were better.\nRaene is correct, I know about Dartol's creation and the treants in the area--at least I did once. They've become corrupted now, their nature twisted.\nIf your goal is to find the next piece of the rod, then you'll have to find the key to open the chest it's in.\nThe wooden key is on one of the treants northeast of here, near Felwood. Once you have it, look for a small glade west of the road near the Felwood border... the chest should be hidden around there.","rew":"Experience: 2,200\n+100 reputation with Darnassus","back":"It upsets me so that the treants have become corrupt. I wish I could do more to help them.","done":"I'm pleased to see you're back, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Ashenvale","x":53.5,"y":46.2,"n":"Shael'dryn","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ashenvale"]},"706":{"id":706,"t":"Fiery Blaze Enchantments","lv":45,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Acquire a Black Drake's Heart for Sigrun Ironhew.\nBlack Drake's Heart Scalding Whelp 2 % , Scorched Guardian 2 %","desc":"As an apprentice to Feranor Steeltoe, I learned his special technique for imbuing weapons with fiery enchantments. Last I heard of him, he was working at a smithy with a hunting party up in Lordaeron.\nI can't tell you too many of the details about the process, but I can tell you it requires blood from a rare, still-beating black drake whelp's heart. I don't have much to do waiting for word from Ironforge. If you bring me a heart from the whelps in Lethlor Ravine, I'll show you my skill!","rew":"You will receive:\nFiery Blaze Enchantment\nExperience: 3,900\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"How goes the hunt, ‹class›?","done":"Ah yes, this will do excellently. This will enable your weapons to strike with searing heat!","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":53.8,"y":43.3,"n":"Sigrun Ironhew","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["badlands"]},"3906":{"id":3906,"t":"Disharmony of Flame","lv":52,"min":48,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Travel to the quarry in Blackrock Mountain and slay Overmaster Pyron. Return to Thunderheart when you have completed this assignment.\nOvermaster Pyron slain","desc":"The elders have felt a disturbance amongst the elements. The Dark Iron dwarves have summoned a foul spirit into our world that threatens to plague our lands with an eternal draught. This disharmony of flame must be investigated.\nTravel to Blackrock Mountain, through the Chasm of Flame, into the quarry. It is there that you shall find this lord of fire: Overmaster Pyron.\nEnd the disruption and return to me.","rew":"Money: 1 55 1 gold, 55 silver, 0 copper Experience: 5,100\n+100 reputation with Thunder Bluff","back":"The elements are still in disarray, ‹name›.","done":"This cannot be... it must not be. The destruction of Pyron has merely lifted a veil. Within the depths of Blackrock is a much more insidious source of corruption.\nBadlands Searing Gorge","pins":[{"z":"Badlands","x":3.3,"y":48.3,"n":"Thunderheart","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-mountain"]},"4866":{"id":4866,"t":"Mother's Milk","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"In the heart of Blackrock Spire you will find Mother Smolderweb. Engage her and get her to poison you. Chances are good that you will have to kill her as well. Return to Ragged John when you are poisoned so that he can 'milk' you.","desc":"It's probably one of the most potent poisons in the world, ‹race›!\nI've overheard the Blackrock speaking about its lethality in my jaunts into the Spire. They call it 'Mother's Milk', named after Mother Smolderweb, the big nasty spider in the Skitterweb cave.\nNow here's what I need from you: A live sample of the Milk, flowing through YOUR veins. Just bringing me the gland won't be enough! Get her to poison you and come back to me!\nThen... I get to milk ya!\n<Rubs his hands together in anticipation.>","rew":"You will receive:\nRagged John's Neverending Cup\nMoney: 1 80 1 gold, 80 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950","back":"<Ragged John pinches you.>","done":"This is gonna make the best ale yet!\nEh, what did you think I was gonna use this for? Poison or something??\nCrazy kids...","pins":[{"z":"Burning Steppes","x":65,"y":23.8,"n":"Ragged John","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["blackrock-spire"]},"96626":{"id":96626,"t":"Camping 101 cooking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Tomas in Goldshire to learn to become a cook.\nLearn cooking from Tomas in Goldshire","desc":"So you want to learn more about camping, huh? Good for you, ‹class›. The first step any adventurer needs to take is to become a cook and learn how to make a campfire.\nCooking's not just about making tasty foods. It's also the foundation for your camp.","back":"A good campfire is the foundation to any good camp.","done":"With this, you'll be able to set up a camp anywhere out in the wilderness. What you've learned is just the basics, so you won't be able to place too many furnishings around it.\nRaise your cooking skill and you might just be able to learn to make even bigger fires.\nYou can also learn the basics of furnishing your campsites from other tradeskill trainers if you're savvy in their skills.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.8,"y":63.2,"n":"Sam Sarsaparilla","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":44.2,"y":66,"n":"Tomas","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"97906":{"id":97906,"t":"Camping 101 leatherworking","lv":6,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Speak with Karolek in Orgrimmar to learn to craft a camping item for your profession once you have shown proficiency in your skill.\nRaise your leatherworking skill to 20","desc":"You've become a leatherworker. Good for you, ‹class›. I reckon I know someone that can teach you how to make yourself a tent that will keep you cool on hot days, and dry on rainy days.\nWith a good tent over your head, you'll ensure that you get all the rest you need to stay sharp on your travels.","done":"There you have it, your very own camp tent. Most folk don't care much for tents being set up in the center of town, so you'll need to head into the wilderness if you want to test it out.\nOh, and just remember, no camp is complete without a campfire. You'll need one of those before you start up your camp. Most cooks can teach you to make a fire. If you haven't already, you might want to check in with someone who can train you in the culinary arts to learn the basics.\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":52,"y":47.4,"n":"Brakk","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":62.8,"y":44.4,"n":"Karolek","e":1}],"cats":["camping"]},"94306":{"id":94306,"t":"Craftsmans writ crimson silk robe","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Crimson Silk Robe\nCrimson Silk Robe","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Crimson Silk Robe, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Crimson Silk Robe Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94306","cats":["crafting"]},"94226":{"id":94226,"t":"Craftsmans writ green iron gauntlets","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever. Its level is not known yet.","obj":"Acquire the items requested by the customer and deliver them to the location marked on your map. This writ must be in your possession to complete the transaction.\nCraftsman's Writ: Green Iron Gauntlets\nGreen Iron Gauntlets","desc":"<Penned in faded ink, the note is requesting $2oa Green Iron Gauntlets, along with information about delivery location and payment. At the bottom appears text denoting this writ is transferable.>\nStart an item: Craftsman's Writ: Green Iron Gauntlets Level 0 , requires level 1 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Quest ID 94226","cats":["crafting"]},"7906":{"id":7906,"t":"Darkmoon cards beasts","min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Beasts Deck\nLevel 0 Difficulty 1 3 Side Both factions Shareable Yes Quest ID 7906","cats":["darkmoon-faire"]},"7506":{"id":7506,"t":"The Emerald Dream...","lv":60,"min":54,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 7,050, 0.94 times as much.","obj":"Return the book to its rightful owners.\nThe Emerald Dream A Dusty Tome 0 % , A Dusty Tome 0 %\nProvided: The Emerald Dream","desc":"The tome carries the mark of the Athenaeum.","rew":"You will receive:\nRoyal Seal of Eldre'Thalas\nExperience: 6,600\n+200 reputation with Shen'dralar","back":"You have recovered a tome!","done":"Excellent work, ‹race›. Should you find any more tomes, do not hesitate to return them to us.\nAs time passes, we tend to change around and even add new rewards for the return of missing tomes.\nStart an item: The Emerald Dream End Lorekeeper Javon Level 60 , requires level 54 Difficulty 54 56 58 Side Human, Orc, Dwarf, Night Elf, Undead, Tauren, Gnome, Troll Class Druid Type Dungeon Shareable No Quest ID 7506","cats":["dire-maul"]},"466":{"id":466,"t":"Search for Incendicite","lv":22,"min":20,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 6 loads of Incendicite Ore to Pilot Stonegear in Dun Morogh.\n6 Incendicite Ore Incendicite Mineral Vein , Incendicite Mineral Vein , Cave Stalker 0.3 % , Leech Stalker 0.2 %","desc":"I heard that a rare ore, incendicite, was found in the Wetlands, in a cave northwest of Algaz Gate. Incendicite is volatile stuff and hard to use without blowing yourself up, but I'm sure if it's smelted the right way it could make cannon shells that pack a mighty punch!\nGet me incendicite ore and I'll find someone brave enough to experiment with it.\nOh, and to extract that ore from a vein you'll need skill in mining. If you don't have it, then ... bring a friend who does to that cave!","rew":"You will receive:\nBeerstained Gloves\nExperience: 1,750\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Where is that ore, ‹name›?!","done":"You got the ore! Well done, ‹name›! I'll get someone to work with this right away. Let's hope he doesn't blow himself up!\nDun Morogh Wetlands","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":49.6,"y":48.6,"n":"Pilot Stonegear","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["dun-morogh"]},"786":{"id":786,"t":"Thwarting Kolkar Aggression","lv":8,"min":5,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Lar Prowltusk outside of Sen'jin Village wants you to destroy the 3 sets of Attack Plans held within Kolkar Crag.\nAttack Plan: Valley of Trials destroyed\nAttack Plan: Sen'jin Village destroyed\nAttack Plan: Orgrimmar destroyed","desc":"Lower your voice, ‹class›. The Kolkar centaurs lie just over the ridge to the west in Kolkar Crag.\nLast night while they were raiding, I snuck into their village and discovered that the dirty beasts have a three-tiered attack planned on the trolls and orcs of Durotar.\nWe mustn't let their invasion come to fruition. Perhaps you can muster the might needed to infiltrate Kolkar Crag and destroy their attack plans.\nLast I saw, they had divided them up amongst three of their leaders.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nSeasoned Fighter's Cloak Heavy Cord Bracers\nExperience: 700\n+100 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+100 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"The centaurs have proven to be a consistent nuisance to the Horde. Their intentions to lay siege to our homeland cannot be tolerated.","done":"The Horde would surely prevail if the Kolkar centaurs were to attack. But by preventing such an attack. we have spared our mighty warriors unnecessary bloodshed.\nAnd as sure as there is sand in the Tanaris desert, we know that there will be blood spilled before these trying times are through.\nYou have served your people well, ‹class›.","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":54.2,"y":73.3,"n":"Lar Prowltusk","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["durotar"]},"226":{"id":226,"t":"Wolves at Our Heels","lv":21,"min":19,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 12 Starving Dire Wolves and 8 Rabid Dire Wolves, then return to Lars at Sven's Camp on the western border of Duskwood.\nStarving Dire Wolf slain : 0/ 12\nRabid Dire Wolf slain : 0/ 8","desc":"Sven and I have dangerous days ahead of us, what with the Necromancer to the east and all. And out here alone as we are, we have to hunt for our own food. It seems every time I'm heading back to camp with some meat on me, starving or rabid dire wolves come out of the forest wanting a bite. It goes without saying, living out here is dangerous work!\nBut if you can rid us of some of those wolves, we'd have an easier time of it. They mostly prowl north and east of here, near the river.","rew":"You will receive:\n5 Flash Bundle\nExperience: 1,250\n+75 reputation with Stormwind","back":"You still hunting wolves...?","done":"Oh good. You thinned out that pack quite a bit, and without those wolves nipping out our heels, we can bind our minds to dealing with Morbent Fel.\nHere, take some of these Flash Bundles. They make them in town, and a lot have been donated to Sven to help with his cause.","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":7.7,"y":33.2,"n":"Lars","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"66":{"id":66,"t":"The Legend of Stalvan","lv":28,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Seek out the Clerk Daltry in the Darkshire Town Hall.","desc":"Last night a horrible disturbance rippled through my veins. I sensed that my granddaughter, Alyssa, was in great danger. I consulted the cards and Death stared up at me from the table.\nAfter taking a long journey through a dark trance I was able to uncover a clue to this terrifying mystery. A name came to me, the name of Stalvan.\nSeek out the Clerk in the Town Hall and see if you can find out more about this character. I fear for us all.","rew":"Experience: 230\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Ah so Madame Eva sent you....","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":75.8,"y":45.3,"n":"Madame Eva","s":1},{"z":"Duskwood","x":72.5,"y":46.9,"n":"Clerk Daltry","e":1}],"cats":["duskwood"]},"9186":{"id":9186,"t":"Craftsman's Writ - Wicked Leather Belt","lv":60,"min":55,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver 9 Wicked Leather Belts and the Craftsman's Writ - Wicked Leather Belt - to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nCraftsman's Writ - Wicked Leather Belt\n9 Wicked Leather Belt\nProvided: Craftsman's Writ - Wicked Leather Belt","desc":"The bearer of this writ is entitled to payment in the form of an insignia of their choice upon completion of the contracted work order.\nWork Order LW-736:\n9 Wicked Leather Belts.\nAll filled orders should be delivered to Packmaster Stonebruiser at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands.\nContract is null and void if tampered with or damaged.\n-Dispatch Commander Metz, The Argent Dawn","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nInsignia of the Crusade Insignia of the Dawn\n+50 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"Filling a work order, ‹class›?","done":"These belts are actually more wicked than the headbands - if you can believe such a thing to be possible.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":70.7,"y":48.5,"n":"Packmaster Stonebruiser","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"6146":{"id":6146,"t":"Nathanos' Ruse","lv":60,"min":56,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 6,850, 0.96 times as much.","obj":"Travel to Tyr's Hand, southeast of the Marris Stead. Once there, take a bite of the Rotten Apple. While under the guise of the Scarlet Crusade, deliver the Grand Crusader's Command to Crusader Lord Valdelmar.\nThe Grand Crusader's Command\nProvided: Nathanos' Chest","desc":"I have made some adjustments to this command. Should our little ruse work, they will expose the Scarlet Oracle and we shall strike!\nNow pay attention, ‹class›. You are to deliver this command to the Crusader Lord, Valdelmar.\nHow? You are going to hand it to him, imbecile.\nTake the command and this rotten apple to Tyr's Hand. When you cross into the city, eat the apple. You will transform into something more... palatable to the humans. Take the command and hand it to the Crusader Lord, Valdelmar.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"This is unacceptable, soldier!","done":"Where have you been? We had thought the Scourge had captured you.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":22.2,"y":63.5,"n":"Nathanos Blightcaller","s":1},{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":75.2,"y":71.2,"n":"Crusader Lord Valdelmar","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"8946":{"id":8946,"t":"Proof of Life","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Ysida's Locket to Anthion Harmon in Eastern Plaguelands.\nYsida's Locket\nProvided: Ysida's Locket","desc":"It is the cruelest of fates that my beloved has perished while trying to rescue me. Yet, you claim to possess the ability to converse with him.\nBring him this locket as proof that I am well. He must not linger in this world; my heart would not be able to bear it.\nFarewell, ‹name›. I shall be in your debt always.","rew":"Experience: 6,600","back":"Ysida... is she alive?","done":"That locket... you found her! I can rest in peace at long last.\nI shall now answer any questions you might have, ‹name›. But make haste, my time in this world is not long.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":26.1,"y":11.3,"n":"Anthion Harmon","e":1}],"cats":["eastern-plaguelands"]},"91746":{"id":91746,"t":"Elmpaws head","lv":10,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Deliver Elmpaw's Head to Helene Peltskinner near Goldshire.\nProvided: Elmpaw's Head","desc":"The trophy serves as an impressive reminder of your victory over Elmpaw. A local hunter or skinner might be interested to hear the story.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 850\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Yes?","done":"So, you took down Elmpaw? Very impressive, Ingmmar!\nLet me give you something in return for your trophy - I know a few collectors who will pay quite well to have this on their mantle once I've prepared it.","pins":[{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":46.2,"y":62.2,"n":"Helene Peltskinner","e":1}],"cats":["elwynn-forest"]},"4466":{"id":4466,"t":"Corrupted Windblossom","lv":55,"min":48,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"2 Cenarion Plant Salve","rew":"Experience: 550","back":"You have found a sickly, corrupted version of what appears to be a windblossom plant. The berries that hang from the plant appear rotten and poisonous. It desperately needs some sort of attention if it is to be turned back to normal.","done":"You apply two Cenarion plant salves to the windblossom. It immediately begins to shed its corrupted form, blossoming into a vibrant and healthy plant.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":36.6,"y":62,"n":"Corrupted Windblossom","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"8466":{"id":8466,"t":"Feathers for Grazle","lv":55,"min":45,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Some of the Deadwood furbolgs wear a distinctive headdress that may be used as a means of proof in thinning their numbers. Bring me a feather from any headdresses you acquire; for every set of five you bring me, you will earn recognition amongst the Timbermaw.\n5 Deadwood Headdress Feather Chieftain Bloodmaw 35 % , Deadwood Shaman 35 % , Deadwood Avenger 35 % , Deadwood Den Watcher 35 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 550\n+50 reputation with Timbermaw Hold","back":"While you have proven yourself to me, you may need to continue to work toward proving yourself to the suspicious brethren of my tribe. To that end, I may be able to continue assisting you.\nSome of the Deadwood furbolgs wear a distinctive headdress that may be used as a means of proof in thinning their numbers. Bring me a feather from any headdresses you acquire; for every set of five you bring me, you will earn recognition amongst the Timbermaw.","done":"Well done, ‹name›! I will make sure that your deeds are known amongst my kind.\nRemember to bring any of the feathers you find to me. I will continue to accept them as long as necessary.","pins":[{"z":"Felwood","x":50.9,"y":85,"n":"Grazle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["felwood"]},"2866":{"id":2866,"t":"The Ruins of Solarsal","lv":43,"min":40,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from The Ruins of Solarsal .","obj":"Explore the Ruins of Solarsal and investigate the presence of the naga there.","desc":"To our south are the Ruins of Solarsal; this is an area that far pre-dates modern times. We explored the ruins initially and found nothing of note; as such, we left it in peace.\nVery recently, the Hatecrest naga have occupied these ruins in alarming numbers. At first, we considered it as the precursor for an attack. Though that threat is still possible, we believe there might be something else going on.\nGo there, explore the ruins, and look for anything that stands out to you. Good luck, ‹name›.","rew":"Experience: 2,700\n+75 reputation with Darnassus","done":"Examining the gazebo reveals some interesting and unusual things in contrast to the surrounding ruins.\nFirst, the gazebo is clearly a more recent construction than the other objects in the ruins. Second, the gazebo has a small series of glyphs engraved into the sides of it; the glyphs repeat in their pattern, but it otherwise is unknown in origin and meaning. Third, the stone of the gazebo itself is warm to the touch.\nThis certainly quantifies as \"standing out\" in the search of the ruins!","pins":[{"z":"Feralas","x":30.3,"y":46.2,"n":"Shandris Feathermoon","s":1},{"z":"Feralas","x":26.3,"y":52.3,"n":"Solarsal Gazebo","e":1}],"cats":["feralas"]},"866":{"id":866,"t":"Root Samples","lv":16,"min":9,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 8 Root Samples to Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.\n8 Root Sample Silverleaf 40 % , Earthroot 40 % , Mageroyal 40 % , Briarthorn 40 % in Razorfen Kraul","desc":"The herbs of the Barrens are not quite like herbs in other lands. Their properties are mostly the same, but the oasis water here alters the plants; they are just slightly different.\nI want to study those differences... to see if they're exploitable!\nIf you are skilled in herbalism, then gather root samples off the herbs you find in the Barrens. Bring back these samples so that I may compare them with herbs from other regions.","rew":"You will receive:\nSpore-covered Tunic\nMoney: 8 0 gold, 8 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,150\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"Hello, ‹name›. Did you get those root samples?","done":"Yes yes, these are very nice! I will grow specimens from these roots and study them. I hope to find new properties from them. Hidden, valuable properties...!\nAnd don't worry -- if I do then you'll be the first to know. Because I'll need someone to gather more!","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.4,"y":37.6,"n":"Mebok Mizzyrix","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["herbalism"]},"546":{"id":546,"t":"Souvenirs of Death","lv":25,"min":20,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deathguard Samsa of Tarren Mill wants 30 Hillsbrad Human Skulls.\n30 Hillsbrad Human Skull Writhing Mage 75 % , Cursed Justicar 75 % , Cursed Paladin 75 % , Condemned Monk 75 % and 4 more","desc":"I hear you were enlisted by Darthalia to wage war on the humans of Hillsbrad. So jealous I am. . .\nWhile you're off having all the fun -- slaying humans, pillaging the town, terrorizing innocent people -- I am stuck standing guard here in Tarren Mill.\nPerhaps you'll take pity on an old Deathguard like myself? You see I am collecting human skulls. And you will be fighting humans for quite some time. Over the course of your long battle, bring me 30 skulls and I will make it worth your while.","rew":"You will receive:\nSkull Ring\nExperience: 2,550\n+150 reputation with Undercity","back":"So the lucky ‹name› returns? How many humans have you slaughtered today? Hundreds I do hope!\nHave you any skulls for me?","done":"Precious skulls! So beautiful! I owe you as promised, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Hillsbrad Foothills","x":62.1,"y":19.7,"n":"Deathguard Samsa","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["hillsbrad-foothills"]},"6066":{"id":6066,"t":"The Hunter's Path","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village.","desc":"Hello, young hunter. You look to me like you are skilled enough to handle a beast and train it as your companion.\nYou must see Yaw Sharpmane in Bloodhoof Village. He can put you on the path to earning a pet of your own.","rew":"Experience: 85","done":"Yes, I do believe you are ready...","pins":[{"z":"Mulgore","x":44,"y":76.4,"n":"Lanka Farshot","s":1},{"z":"Mulgore","x":46.9,"y":59.6,"n":"Yaw Sharpmane","e":1}],"cats":["hunter"]},"2946":{"id":2946,"t":"Seeing What Happens","lv":50,"min":45,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring the miniature platinum discs to the gates of Uldum in Tanaris and look for clues as to the connection between the two.\nMiniature Platinum Discs\nProvided: Miniature Platinum Discs","desc":"We want you to take the miniature discs you found to the sealed gates of Uldum. We... we aren't sure what will happen when you do this.\nThis sounds risky, sure, we acknowledge that. It might, however, do nothing. You might need to use the discs on something. Perhaps the doors unlock when you have the discs in your possession. Be open to try anything, and be ready for anything to happen.\nWhen you've found out what happens, return to Ironforge. We'll have a lot to analyze when you're done!","rew":"Experience: 4,700\n+100 reputation with Ironforge","back":"This familiar looking pedestal sticks out of the hot sand. Perhaps there is something to its presence here...","done":"As you touch the pedestal, the miniature discs from Uldaman hum and glow in your backpack. A familiar feeling tingle washes over your hands, as the image of another Stone Watcher springs to life in front of the gates of Uldum.\n\"Salutations. I am a guardian of entry. The discs that have been used for access are missing the correct entry discs, the Plates of Uldum. Please incorporate these plates with the disc structure and repeat your access sequencing. Thank you.\"\nDun Morogh Tanaris","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":63.5,"y":23,"n":"Historian Karnik","s":1},{"z":"Tanaris","x":37.6,"y":81.4,"n":"Uldum Pedestal","e":1}],"cats":["ironforge"]},"8866":{"id":8866,"t":"Bronzebeard the Elder","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nCoin of Ancestry\n+50 reputation with Horde\n+50 reputation with Alliance","done":"It is good to know the people of this land still pay homage to the olden races. I bid you well, ‹name›, and offer you this token...","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":55.8,"y":23.8,"n":"Elder Bronzebeard","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["lunar-festival"]},"9106":{"id":9106,"t":"Plagueheart Shoulderpads","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Mataus the Wrathcaster at Light's Hope Chapel in the Eastern Plaguelands will make Plagueheart Shoulderpads if you bring him the following: 1 Desecrated Shoulderpads, 12 Wartorn Cloth Scraps, 2 Mooncloth and 3 Cured Rugged Hides.\nDesecrated Shoulderpads Grobbulus 0 % in Naxxramas , Gluth 0 % in Naxxramas , Patchwerk 0 % in Naxxramas\n12 Wartorn Cloth Scrap Stoneskin Gargoyle 35 % in Naxxramas , Infectious Ghoul 30.3 % in Naxxramas , Bile Retcher 28.5 % in Naxxramas , Mad Scientist 28.3 % in Naxxramas and 4 more\n2 Mooncloth\n3 Cured Rugged Hide","desc":"I make no pretenses, maggot. The darkness Plagueheart items hold could very well destroy the both of us. That is why the price is so high. If I'm going to die, it's going to be as a rich man.\nAnd I don't give an ounce of gnoll spit how you die, only that you do as I ask. Bring me what I require and we will both benefit - or die; but I've already explained this...","rew":"You will receive:\nPlagueheart Shoulderpads\n+200 reputation with Argent Dawn","back":"You got some missing parts for the quest please go and get them all!","done":"Exellent ‹name› !\n, you got everything just as i asked and now i can make a Plagueheart Shoulderpads.","pins":[{"z":"Eastern Plaguelands","x":71.6,"y":48.7,"n":"Mataus the Wrathcaster","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["naxxramas"]},"3506":{"id":3506,"t":"Betrayed","lv":56,"min":44,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Destroy the arcane focusing crystal tied to Magus Rimtori and then slay her. Afterwards, take the Head of Magus Rimtori to Ag'tor Bloodfist in Azshara.\nHead of Magus Rimtori Magus Rimtori","desc":"A few more moments of thought brings a few ideas to mind, one of which brings a smile to your face: perhaps destroying the crystals would upset the blood elf responsible for the slaughter of so many orcs and the betrayal of Belgrom?\nYou continue to decipher more of the script and pictures and realize that one of the crystals is tied to the creator of the circle--the others are tied to something far more sinister.\nYou close the book and begin to decide which crystal to destroy.","rew":"Experience: 4,350\n+75 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"How goes your slaughter of the blood elf traitors, ‹name›? Have you made any progress?\nI hope you are the one strong enough to bring that dog to her knees! She deserves nothing but a painful death for all that she has done!","done":"RAR!! Incredible!\nYou've done it! Belgrom will be pleased! Finally the spirits of dozens of our warriors can be at peace. Thank you, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Azshara","x":59.5,"y":31.3,"n":"Kaldorei Tome of Summoning","s":1},{"z":"Azshara","x":22.3,"y":51.5,"n":"Ag'tor Bloodfist","e":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7826":{"id":7826,"t":"A Donation of Wool","lv":60,"min":12,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"60 Wool Cloth Farrin Daris 66.7 % , Adam Lind 62.1 % , Mountaineer Langarr 57.1 % , Protector Leick 47.6 % and 4 more","rew":"Experience: 650\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"If you have the sixty pieces of wool cloth on you and are ready to donate them, I'm able to take them from you now.","done":"Wonderful! We thank you for your generous donation, ‹name›!","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":63.6,"y":51.2,"n":"Rashona Straglash","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["orgrimmar"]},"7666":{"id":7666,"t":"Again Into the Great Ossuary","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","rew":"You will receive:\nDivination Scryer","done":"Are you headed back into the Scholomance, ‹name›? You've already paid such a great price for the use of the Divination Scryer - perhaps you'd like to take another one with you. With it, you'd be able to face the perils of the Great Ossuary once more.\nBy all means, have it. You've certainly earned it.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":48.4,"y":50.2,"n":"Lord Grayson Shadowbreaker","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["paladin"]},"6626":{"id":6626,"t":"A Host of Evil","lv":35,"min":28,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 8 Razorfen Battleguard, 8 Razorfen Thornweavers, and 8 Death's Head Cultists and return to Myriam Moonsinger near the entrance to Razorfen Downs.\nRazorfen Battleguard slain : 0/ 8\nRazorfen Thornweaver slain : 0/ 8\nDeath's Head Cultist slain : 0/ 8","desc":"The Forsaken do not pass on their... illness... from what I have seen. This diplomat seems to be granting undeath to would-be followers. I am beginning to think he is one of the Scourge.\nFor now, my concern is not with him though, it's with the growing ranks around him. They creep from the shadows daily, almost begging him for more power.\nI'm not powerful enough to fight them on my own, ‹name›. What do you say? Are you up for some hunting?","rew":"Money: 75 0 gold, 75 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,450","back":"How goes the hunt, ‹name›? Seeing just this small sample of this diplomat's power here removes any doubt I had that the Scourge are one of the greatest threats this world has ever seen.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›! The work you've done will be a great help, I'm sure.\nI will continue my study of this diplomat and the rest of the quilboar here. If you seek greater adventure, I'd find a few friends and head into the cave that looks like a great boar maw just over there. I'm sure once you're inside you'll find greater challenges to face.\nThe Barrens Thousand Needles","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":49,"y":94.9,"n":"Myriam Moonsinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["razorfen-downs"]},"146":{"id":146,"t":"Messenger to Darkshire","lv":18,"min":18,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Magistrate Solomon with Lord Ebonlocke's letter of response.\nEbonlocke's Response to Solomon\nProvided: Ebonlocke's Response to Solomon","desc":"If I did not know Magistrate Solomon personally, I would say the man has gone mad. Send the Night Watch to Lakeshire because Stormwind refuses aid? The Night Watch was formed because Stormwind left us when this foul magic seeped into the land. If I sent my Night Watch, this town would be overrun by evil before the guards even reached the forest's edge.\nTake this letter of response to your Master in Lakeshire.","rew":"Money: 2 50 0 gold, 2 silver, 50 copper Experience: 340\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Ah, good to see you back, messenger. Shall I inform the Marshal that the Night Watch is on its way from Darkshire?","done":"By the Light! The Stormwind Army retreated from Westfall. And the Guard no longer protects Darkshire? There is some treachery abound. How could this be so?\nOh I forgot to reward your service, ‹class›. Here are some coins. Now excuse me. Something is amiss in Stormwind and I must get to the bottom of it.\nDuskwood Redridge Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Duskwood","x":71.9,"y":46.4,"n":"Lord Ello Ebonlocke","s":1},{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":24.9,"y":44.5,"n":"Magistrate Solomon","e":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"98386":{"id":98386,"t":"Althers mill","lv":21,"min":15,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Slay 12 Greater Tarantulas and destroy 6 Tarantula Eggs in Alther's Mill for Foreman Oslow in Redridge.\nGreater Tarantula slain (12) Greater Tarantula Greater Tarantula Greater Tarantula\nGreater Tarantula\nGreater Tarantula\nGreater Tarantula\nTarantula Egg destroyed : 0/ 6","desc":"Orcs, gnolls, murlocs. Everything seems to be out to stop me from getting this bridge done on time. Now we have word there's an infestation of tarantulas at our lumber mill!\nIf you're up to earn a bit more coin, would you head over to Alther's Mill to the east and clear out their spider problem? Place is as good as useless to me if I can't safely send workers to collect shipments.\nOh, and if you see ol' Alther, tell him he owes me for cleaning up his mess.","rew":"Money: 13 0 gold, 13 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,650\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","done":"The mill is that bad? That's worse than I thought.\nI'm not particularly squeamish, but work's bad enough without spiders snatching up my workers. Thanks for the help,Raton!","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":32.2,"y":48.6,"n":"Foreman Oslow","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["redridge-mountains"]},"96786":{"id":96786,"t":"The syndicate sting","lv":34,"min":24,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Break up the secret deal, and take the object being traded to the Syndicate. Then, return to Myrokos Silentform at Ravenholdt Manor.\nIntercepted Shipment\nSyndicate Uniform","desc":"Falconcrest sent some guys to do a handoff at the southern part of Thoradin's wall. I don't know what they're picking up. Must be good, because everyone involved has kept it a total secret. I don't think the guys picking it up even know what it is.\nThat's all I've got. Don't make me regret telling you that.","rew":"Money: 70 0 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 3,350\n+300 reputation with Ravenholdt\nLevel 34 , requires level 24 Difficulty 24 30 32 37 43 Side Both factions Class Rogue Shareable Yes Quest ID 96786","cats":["rogue"]},"9026":{"id":9026,"t":"Tracing the Source","lv":60,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Innkeeper Allison at The Gilded Rose in Stormwind's Trade District.","desc":"We've got to find the source. I've seen a lot more people than usual - guards included - going in and out of The Gilded Rose. Talk to Allison. If she's selling them, she can tell you where they came from.","done":"Oh yes, I just got the perfume and cologne in stock recently. It's been selling so well, I don't know how long I can keep it on the shelves.\nIf you ask me, it's kind of boring. Everyone smelling the same? It smells great, but still.","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":61.9,"y":75,"n":"Aristan Mottar","s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":60.4,"y":75.3,"n":"Innkeeper Allison","e":1}],"cats":["seasonal"]},"94466":{"id":94466,"t":"Call of fire","lv":14,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring 1 Fire Tar and 1 Reagent Pouch to Braldir Ashmantle in Loch Modan.\nFire Tar\nReagent Pouch","desc":"Bah, ye didn't trek all this way for tales, did ye, ‹name›? Ye seek the Eternal Flame and the fire totem.\nFirst, ye'll need a sapta to bind yer spirit to the flame.\nI'll craft it--but I'll need two things: fire tar from Tunnel Rat Geomancers in the kobold caves up north, and a reagent pouch from a Stonesplinter Seer lurkin' in the southern hills. Dangerous work, but worthy of the flame.","rew":"You will receive:\nFire Sapta\nExperience: 975","back":"Aye, I've near all I need for the fire sapta, Ukko--just missin' the fire tar and the seer's pouch. The tar's carried by Tunnel Rat Geomancers in the kobold caves up north. The pouch ye'll need to wrest from a Stonesplinter seer in the southern hills. These ingredients are bound to flame, as all true saptas must be. Their elemental ties make our craft strong.","done":"These'll do fine, Ukko.\nFire ain't just fury and ruin--mark me words. It's life, it's forge, it's the breath o' creation. All things are bound in balance. One force tempers the other, gives it meaning. Without shadow, light's but a glare. Without flame, stone's but cold memory.\nMasterin' magic means knowin' when to blend, not just burn. That's true wisdom, lad.","pins":[{"z":"Loch Modan","x":32,"y":66,"n":"Braldir Ashmantle","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["shaman"]},"8786":{"id":8786,"t":"Arms for the Field","lv":60,"min":60,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Massive Iron Axes to Merok Longstride at the Orgrimmar Legion camp outside of Hive'Regal. You must also bring Logistics Task Briefing VI in order to complete this quest.\n3 Massive Iron Axe\nLogistics Task Briefing VI\nProvided: Logistics Task Briefing VI","desc":"The Orgrimmar Legion has put in a request for additional weapons that we haven't been able to provide at the moment. Obtain the weapons they've requested and bring them to Merok Longstride outside of Hive'Regal.","rew":"You will receive:\nCenarion Logistics Badge Followup Logistics Assignment\nExperience: 650\n+50 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"You have something for me, ‹name›?","done":"Excellent work. We were in short supply of these, ‹name›.","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":51.9,"y":68,"n":"Merok Longstride","e":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"8306":{"id":8306,"t":"Into The Maw of Madness","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Pays 2g 70s instead of 1g 80s.","obj":"Commander Mar'alith at Cenarion Hold in Silithus wants you to find his beloved Natalia. The information that you gathered points to Hive'Regal in the south as being the area in which you may find Mistress Natalia Mar'alith.\nDo not forget to visit the dwarves at Bronzebeard's camp before venturing into the hive. They might have some additional work and advice for you.\nAnd ‹name›, remember the Commander's words: \"Do what you must...\"\nThe Fate of Mistress Natalia Mar'alith","desc":"I need you to venture into Hive'Regal and find what became of my dearest Natalia, ‹name›. This will be no easy task for you. Before you dive headlong into the maw of madness, make sure that you go back and speak with those dwarves. They might be able to give you some tips on dealing with the silithid that inhabit that hive.\nAnd ‹name›, if she truly is as mad as they say... do what you must.\n<Commander Mar'alith turns away from you.>","rew":"You will receive:\nCorrupted Blackwood Staff\nMoney: 2 70 2 gold, 70 silver, 0 copper Experience: 9,950\n+200 reputation with Cenarion Circle","back":"Natalia?","done":"<Commander Mar'alith clutches at his chest.>\nC'Thun? WHAT is the meaning of all this? What is C'Thun? How could this fiend have turned my sweet Natalia into the monster that you described?","pins":[{"z":"Silithus","x":49.2,"y":34.2,"n":"Commander Mar'alith","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["silithus"]},"78146":{"id":78146,"t":"Goaz scrolls","lv":20,"min":1,"side":"Both","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Goaz Scrolls","rew":"You will receive:\nItem 211779\nMoney: 1 25 0 gold, 1 silver, 25 copper Experience: 160","back":"Have you brought something to add to our collection?\nGoaz Scrolls (1)","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. Our knowledge expands through your efforts.\nIf you discover more magical works that might benefit the library, please bring them to me.\nStormwind City Undercity","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":37.8,"y":80.2,"n":"Garion Wendell","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Undercity","x":73.6,"y":33,"n":"Owen Thadd","e":1}],"cats":["special"]},"1266":{"id":1266,"t":"The Missing Diplomat","lv":36,"min":28,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Find Private Hendel in Dustwallow Marsh.","desc":"Private Hendel is to the west of here. He's currently on guard duty protecting some of Theramore's infiltrators while they rest. They've been keeping tabs on the Horde base, Brackenwall, and looking for anything else that might threaten our borders.\nYou should have no problem finding him; just look for the tents along the road.\nI have another matter to attend to, but I shall catch up to you soon enough. You can always find me in the Lady Proudmoore's tower if you have any problems.","rew":"Experience: 700\n+25 reputation with Stormwind","done":"Hello, citizen. This is a dangerous place to be wandering about. I wouldn't hang around too long if you value your life.\nIf you keep your questions short, I'll see if I can help you. Just keep your eyes open for any of those filthy ogres. Rumor has it there's a Horde base somewhere in the swamps. The infiltrators are doing what they can to find it, but the process has been slow going and we've had little progress.","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":66.4,"y":49.3,"n":"Archmage Tervosh","s":1},{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":45.2,"y":24.7,"n":"Private Hendel","e":1}],"cats":["stormwind-city"]},"626":{"id":626,"t":"Cortello's Riddle","lv":51,"min":35,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Solve the riddle!","desc":"To Lordaeron! The great land of turmoil\nWhere brave soldiers with death do toil\nFind your way through the great unrest\nThere you will find the end to this quest\nAlong the coast of the Hinterlands, at the base of the great falls\nUnderneath the water there does your treasure call!","rew":"You will receive:\nExplorer's Knapsack\nExperience: 6,100","done":"You open the chest to discover....\nDustwallow Marsh The Hinterlands","pins":[{"z":"Dustwallow Marsh","x":31.1,"y":66.1,"n":"Musty Scroll","s":1},{"z":"The Hinterlands","x":80.8,"y":46.8,"n":"Cortello's Treasure","e":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"8066":{"id":8066,"t":"Paragons of Power: The Predator's Belt","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60. Gives 6,600 experience instead of 9,550, 0.69 times as much.","obj":"Bring the following Paragons of Power from Zul'Gurub to Falthir the Sightless: A Primal Hakkari Shawl. You must also have a reputation equal to or greater than Honored with the Zandalar Tribe.\nFalthir the Sightless is located on Yojamba Isle, Stranglethorn Vale.\nPrimal Hakkari Shawl\nReach 9000 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","desc":"A predator knows how to stalk their prey, but a successful one knows how to strike at it once they have closed ranks. You must master both to have any chance of success in Zul'Gurub... and any chance of being like the Zandalar predators.\nBring me choice parts of the Paragons of Power from within Zul'Gurub. My reward will be the power that the trinkets yield, while yours will be the Zandalar predator's belt - equipment well worth the trade.","rew":"You will receive:\nZandalar Predator's Belt\nExperience: 6,600\n+150 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Strike at the insane minions of Hakkar in Zul'Gurub - they are the ones that hold the Paragons of Power, ‹name›. Prove your success to them - and to the tribe - as an aspirant to the predator.","done":"I sensed your arrival moments before, ‹name›, but none too easily. What revealed yourself to me were the Paragons of Power you brought. I can feel the power without needing to see the trinkets; their latent mojo - raw magic, if you will - will continue to fuel our efforts of vanquishing the diabolic schemes of the Blood God Hakkar.\nYou are to be commended - and rewarded - for your success. You are honored amongst the tribe, and you are worthy to wear the predator's belt.","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["stranglethorn-vale"]},"4146":{"id":4146,"t":"Zapper Fuel","lv":52,"min":47,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Deliver the Unloaded Zapper and 5 samples of Atal'ai Haze to Larion in Marshal's Refuge.\nUnloaded Zapper\n5 Atal'ai Haze Deep Lurker 80 % , Saturated Ooze 40 % , Murk Worm 40 %\nProvided: Unloaded Zapper","desc":"You're in luck, ‹name›! I've been working on some of my own experiments while Marvon's been gone, and one of them is a short range bug zapper. With just a few adjustments, it should be great for ridding yourself of those Bloodpetal pests.\nI can let you have one of my zapper prototypes, but you'll still need to collect the fuel. You can get the necessary Atal'ai haze that the zapper needs in the temple of Atal'Hakkar. The deep lurkers, murk worms, or oozes are the ones you'll need to get it from.","rew":"Experience: 5,100","back":"This is exhausting, ‹name›. Those things just won't leave me alone!","done":"So, Marvon wasn't around? Well, show me what you got, anyway.\nThe Barrens Un'Goro Crater","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.4,"y":38.7,"n":"Liv Rizzlefix","s":1},{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":45.5,"y":8.7,"n":"Larion","e":1}],"cats":["sunken-temple"]},"1426":{"id":1426,"t":"Threat From the Sea","lv":43,"min":35,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Kill 10 Marsh Murlocs, 10 Marsh Inkspewer, and 10 Marsh Flesheater, then return to Katar in the Swamp of Sorrows.\nMarsh Murloc slain : 0/ 10\nMarsh Inkspewer slain : 0/ 10\nMarsh Flesheater slain : 0/ 10","desc":"I have no love for the sea, nor any creature I've seen come from its depths. It is a powerful but blind mistress; callous and brutal. It would bring me great pleasure to slay the fish men by the hundreds if it were within my power. But I garner some pleasure from watching their deaths at the hands of any who do the Horde's will.\nWhich brings us to you, ‹class›. How many can you slay? Would you test yourself against their most powerful kind?","rew":"Experience: 4,450\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar","back":"I am patient. Patient and everlasting like an old kank stone from Draenor. The fish men shall not make it past our borders--not while I still stand. If we had an army at our disposal I would cleanse this world and all others of their presence. I feel my hatred seethe just speaking about them.","done":"The sea seems vast and relentless, but you have stained her with the blood of her own spawn. The fish men know pain. Their stupidity will force them to refortify their ranks from the devastation you've caused, and that is good.\nLet their gurgling screams overshadow the sea's roar long into the night. I shall smile every time I hear one of them silenced.\nReturn to me if you wish to slay more of the fish men. I will gladly reward you again.\nSwamp of Sorrows Blasted Lands","pins":[{"z":"Swamp of Sorrows","x":83.8,"y":80.4,"n":"Katar","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["swamp-of-sorrows"]},"6386":{"id":6386,"t":"Return to the Crossroads.","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Renamed from Return to the Crossroads.","obj":"Buy a wind rider to the Crossroads from the wind rider master Doras, then bring Gryshka's Letter to Zargh at the Crossroads.\nGryshka's Letter\nProvided: Gryshka's Letter","desc":"My wind riders are trained to fly to many different places, as long as you have already been to that place and spoken with the wind rider master there.\nYou have been to the Crossroads and spoken to their wind rider master Devrak, so now you can fly directly to him from here. Once you're at the Crossroads, you can deliver Gryshka's letter to Zargh.\nSpeak with me when you are ready to go.","rew":"Money: 3 50 0 gold, 3 silver, 50 copper Experience: 1,050\n+150 reputation with Orgrimmar\n+150 reputation with Darkspear Trolls","back":"Have you returned from Orgrimmar? Did Gryshka like the meat I sent her?","done":"Hah! I guess she liked it! Nothing brings red to a lady's cheeks like a big, juicy steak!\nThank you, ‹name›. You've done me a great service. Here is some money for your trouble, and don't be surprised if I invite you to my wedding!\nOrgrimmar The Barrens","pins":[{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":45.1,"y":63.9,"n":"Doras","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":52.6,"y":29.8,"n":"Zargh","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"92706":{"id":92706,"t":"Wanted bruuz","lv":20,"min":15,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring Bruuz's Dorsal Fin to Gazlowe in Ratchet.\nBruuz's Dorsal Fin","desc":"Calling all anglers!\nA giant shark has been circling the waters near the shipping dock, attacking sailors and small boats. Dockworkers have given it the nickname \"Bruuz\". A hefty reward will be given to whoever brings me its fin!\n-- Gazlowe","rew":"Money: 25 0 gold, 25 silver, 0 copper Experience: 1,950\n+100 reputation with Ratchet","back":"What can I do for ya, ‹race›?","done":"Finally, somebody killed that thing! Do you know how hard it is to get a crew in the water when everyone in town's crying \"Shark!\"all the time?\nI might just put that monster's fin into a soup for dinner tonight, just to have the last laugh.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":37.5,"n":"WANTED","s":1},{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.6,"y":36.2,"n":"Gazlowe","e":1}],"cats":["the-barrens"]},"386":{"id":386,"t":"What Comes Around...","lv":25,"min":22,"side":"Alliance","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Gives 4,200 experience instead of 2,000, 2.1 times as much. New rewards: Ursine Hammer. Read from what the game server sent. Its experience counts the level 30 build, which halved what dungeon quests give beyond a normal","obj":"Bring the head of Targorr the Dread to Guard Berton in Lakeshire.\nHead of Targorr Targorr the Dread","desc":"Targorr the Dread served under Gath'Ilzogg as supreme Executioner. His methods were ruthless, even by filthy orc standards. Men who fought bravely to defend the Kingdom were tortured on his whim. Now he is being held in the Stormwind Stockade, sentenced to die. Yet something is amiss. One of the bureaucratic nobles put a hold on his execution. I am sure foul play is in the works.\nPut an end to Targorr the Dread, ‹name›. Travel to The Stockade and behead him before trickery is upon us.","rew":"You will be able to choose one of these rewards:\nLucine Longsword Hardened Root Staff Ursine Hammer\nNew in Forever: Ursine Hammer.\nExperience: 4,200\n+100 reputation with Stormwind","back":"Have you been to Stormwind yet, to The Stockade? I fear whatever trickery that has kept Targorr the Dread alive for this long will eventually bring about his freedom. He was sentenced to die, ‹name›, not act as some political pawn on a noble's whim.","done":"Targorr the Dread has finally met his fate. I for one am glad to hear the beast now knows what it is like to be on the receiving end of Death's ruthless grip. You have done well, ‹name›. Sometimes the truest justice can only be found outside the courtroom and beyond the clouded vision of politics.","pins":[{"z":"Redridge Mountains","x":21.2,"y":46.6,"n":"Guard Berton","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["the-stockade"]},"1106":{"id":1106,"t":"Martek the Exiled","lv":35,"min":26,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring Fizzle's Letter to Martek the Exiled in the Badlands.\nFizzle Brassbolts' Letter\nProvided: Fizzle Brassbolts' Letter","desc":"I'm developing a new engine that'll make the car go so fast! Fast enough to fly, I know it! I just need to make pistons that can handle very very heavy stress. All my trials have failed because I can't make pistons hard enough!\nBut there is someone who might know how.\nHis name is Martek the Exiled. He is a great smith and knows more about metal than anyone. Take him this letter, I know he can help!\nBut he's far far away -- in Azeroth, in the Badlands, in a camp, with a goblin!\nFind him!","rew":"Experience: 1,350","back":"Well, you found me. Good for you.\nAre you here about that axe I made for Gath'Ilzogg? Or are you here to reclaim Duchess Pamay's honor?\nActually, I don't care which it is. If you're here to fight, then let's get it over with...","done":"Fizzle sent you? Well that changes things! Of course I'll help you. Fizzle and his brother are two of the few people who don't want me dead!\nSo Fizzle wants to make pistons, eh? Pistons strong enough to take whatever stresses he has planned, and if I know Fizzle, then this new car of his is a volcano on wheels!\nThousand Needles Badlands","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":78.1,"y":77.1,"n":"Fizzle Brassbolts","s":1},{"z":"Badlands","x":42.2,"y":52.7,"n":"Martek the Exiled","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"1186":{"id":1186,"t":"The Eighteenth Pilot","lv":37,"min":29,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Razzeric on the Shimmering Flats.","desc":"I'm going to be busy with working on integrating this new fuel regulator to our racer designs, but if you'd like to help out the team some more, talk to Razzeric. He's our pilot--well, our eighteenth pilot, to be exact--and he likes to add his own little modifications to the racers.\nHe's a little off his rocker, though, so try not to act too surprised.","rew":"Experience: 290","done":"You're the ‹race› that's been helping Pozzik out, right? I was like you once, running around the pit area, helping with whatever work the mechanics would let me do.\nNow look at me! The goblin racing team's pilot extraordinaire!","pins":[{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.2,"y":75.9,"n":"Pozzik","s":1},{"z":"Thousand Needles","x":80.3,"y":76.1,"n":"Razzeric","e":1}],"cats":["thousand-needles"]},"4386":{"id":4386,"t":"Crystal Spire","lv":53,"min":47,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"10 Blue Power Crystal Blue Power Crystal , Blue Power Crystal , Mor'vek 25.6 % , Plated Stegodon 0.3 % and 4 more\n10 Yellow Power Crystal Yellow Power Crystal , Yellow Power Crystal , Mor'vek 66.7 % , Gruff 0.6 % and 4 more","rew":"You will receive:\n6 Crystal Spire","back":"The Pylon table allows you to combine blue power crystals with yellow power crystals.\nAccording to J.D.'s manual, this combination can be used to create a shield that does damage to enemies.","done":"Arranging the crystals on the table, you carefully align the colors. As you push the last one into place, a burst of light fuses the crystals together.\nThe resulting combination is now yours.","pins":[{"z":"Un'Goro Crater","x":77.2,"y":50,"n":"Eastern Crystal Pylon","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["ungoro-crater"]},"1506":{"id":1506,"t":"Gan'rul's Summons","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Horde","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Gan'rul Bloodeye in Orgrimmar.","desc":"You there. ‹name›, right?\nI hope your schedule isn't busy, because Gan'rul wants to see you right away. You'll find him with the senior warlocks in the Cleft of Shadow.\nBased on my past dealings with Gan'rul, your summons is either a very good thing or a very bad thing.","rew":"Experience: 210","done":"Good. I was afraid Ophek wouldn't reach you.\nIt is time that I further your warlock training. Any business you have currently will have to wait.\nI trust there will not be a problem with this?\nDurotar Orgrimmar","pins":[{"z":"Durotar","x":54.4,"y":41.3,"n":"Ophek","s":1},{"z":"Orgrimmar","x":48.2,"y":45.3,"n":"Gan'rul Bloodeye","e":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"4786":{"id":4786,"t":"The Completed Robe","lv":38,"min":31,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Wait for Menara Voidrender to complete your robe and then speak to her again.","desc":"I will put the robe together for you now. It will take but a few moments. Do not go far.","rew":"You will receive:\nEnchanted Gold Bloodrobe\nExperience: 3,550","back":"A moment, ‹name›...","done":"It is done, ‹name›. Here you are. Wear it with pride.\nYou've worked hard and I see great things in your future. Remember, to defy the corruption that comes with our path takes great will and fortitude. As long as your will is your own, then you shall have great success.","pins":[{"z":"The Barrens","x":62.5,"y":35.4,"n":"Menara Voidrender","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warlock"]},"3106":{"id":3106,"t":"Simple Rune","lv":1,"min":1,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Read the Simple Rune and speak to Thran Khorman in Coldridge Valley.\nSimple Rune\nProvided: Simple Rune","desc":"While you were helping me out, this rune was given to me to pass on to you. Take some time to read it when you have a chance. I'm thinkin' it came from the warrior trainer Thran. Take a gander at it and go find him inside Anvilmar when you've a chance.","rew":"Experience: 40\n+50 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Blast it's cold today, aint it? It's like the snow never goes away, ‹name›.\nYou've probably noticed already, but there are gnomes now living in our city. That's because they went and got themselves blown out of their own home. Don't go spreadin' this 'round, but I can hardly blame them--I think I woulda resorted to explosives too if Ironforge were infested with Dark Irons or the like.","done":"Other things you'll probably see too, just so yer in the know: dwarves usin' magic in a fight 'stead of a rifle. Some of us takin' to worshippin' the Holy Light like some of the humans, and, last but not least, troggs. You'll learn more 'bout them later, but what you need to know now is that I'm here to help ya.\nI be here to teach ya how to be a real warrior. Anytime ya think ya need more trainin', come back to me and I'll see what I can do.","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":29.9,"y":71.2,"n":"Sten Stoutarm","s":1},{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":28.8,"y":67.2,"n":"Thran Khorman","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"1666":{"id":1666,"t":"Marshal Haggard","lv":10,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Speak with Marshal Haggard.","desc":"You've learned a few moves, but you could still use a decent weapon. I bet if you spoke with Marshal Haggard he could help you.\nMarshal Haggard lives in a manor in Elwynn Forest, at the Eastvale Lumber Camp. He's retired now but he collected a lot of gear during his career.\nLet him know I sent you, and with luck he'll have a spare weapon to offer.","rew":"Experience: 420","done":"Who's that?\nBurlguard, is that you?\nYou'll have to step a little closer. My eyes aren't what they used to be.\nWalking up like that, I thought you were a gnoll!\nStormwind City Elwynn Forest","pins":[{"z":"Stormwind City","x":77.1,"y":53.3,"n":"Harry Burlguard","s":1},{"z":"Elwynn Forest","x":84.6,"y":69.4,"n":"Marshal Haggard","e":1}],"cats":["warrior"]},"8386":{"id":8386,"t":"Fight for Warsong Gulch","lv":19,"min":10,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Bring 3 Warsong Gulch Marks of Honor to an Alliance Brigadier General outside the battlegrounds.\n3 Warsong Gulch Mark of Honor","desc":"The Silverwing Sentinels are at war with the Warsong Outriders due to the destruction the Orcs are causing to the forest. There are, however, more reasons to defend this particular forest than plain love for nature.\nThe forest forms a strategic barrier that makes Ashenvale defendable against a large-scale attack. Without it, Astranaar would last a day or two before being annexed to the Barrens.\nDo your part in fighting the Warsong Outriders, ‹name›! For the Alliance!","rew":"Experience: 725\n+50 reputation with Silverwing Sentinels","back":"You've come back with news from the front, ‹name›?","done":"Well done, ‹name›! You've served the Alliance well.\nDun Morogh Darnassus Stormwind City","pins":[{"z":"Dun Morogh","x":62.3,"y":35.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Darnassus","x":58,"y":34.2,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1},{"z":"Stormwind City","x":81.2,"y":38.5,"n":"Alliance Brigadier General","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["warsong-gulch"]},"306":{"id":306,"t":"In Search of The Excavation Team","lv":24,"min":21,"side":"Alliance","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"Return to Tarrel Rockweaver with Merrin's note.\nMerrin's Letter\nProvided: Merrin's Letter","desc":"It was horrible! We were uncovering some rare artifacts and we began to discover these large bones.\nBefore we knew what was happening, these Mottled Raptors overwhelmed the dig site. Many lives were lost.\nOrmer here -- so brave -- saved the Prospector and me. He defended us as we ran for shelter. Now we are trapped. And our hard work lies in ruin.\nHere, take this note back to my sweet Tarrel. It will explain the situation to him.","rew":"Experience: 490\n+25 reputation with Ironforge","back":"Were you able to find Merrin? Did she send word?","done":"Such horrible news! At least 3 of them survived. But when will the killing end? I long for the day when King Magni's subjects can live without fear.","pins":[{"z":"Wetlands","x":38.9,"y":52.3,"n":"Merrin Rockweaver","s":1},{"z":"Wetlands","x":11.5,"y":52.2,"n":"Tarrel Rockweaver","e":1}],"cats":["wetlands"]},"9266":{"id":9266,"t":"Making Amends","lv":60,"min":40,"side":"Both","tag":"classic","st":"Unchanged in Forever as far as is known: the text, objectives and rewards below are Classic’s.","obj":"40 Runecloth Stormwind Royal Guard , Honor Guard , Skullsplitter Speaker in Zul'Gurub , General Marcus Jonathan 85.7 % and 4 more\n4 Coal Dalaran Miner , Blazing Elemental 28.4 % , Inferno Elemental 24.7 % , Molten Giant 24.7 % and 4 more","back":"You must've done something really bad to us or our friends, ‹name›. At any rate, I'm here to offer you a way to get our good graces back.\nAs you know, Winterspring is quite cold. With so many of us goblins coming from other cities, we could use a hand keeping warm. Bring me some runecloth and coal and I'll put in the good word for ya. Be warned though, our enemies are not going to take kindly to your helping us.","done":"Thank you, ‹name›. You're on a quick path to redeeming yourself with our fair town.","pins":[{"z":"Winterspring","x":59.8,"y":39.7,"n":"Bronn Fitzwrench","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["winterspring"]},"92466":{"id":92466,"t":"Call of earth","lv":4,"min":3,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Bring a Signet of Akir to Windshaper Boro.\nSignet of Akir","desc":"While we owe much of our prosperity to the elements of wind, the path we walk requires that we obey the call of all four of the primary elements and undertake a trial for each. Before you begin your first trial in earnest however, you must prove the strength of your resolve.\nTravel to the standing stones to the east. A force of Al'Aketh converts has been spotted there and they must be driven off. Confront the cultists there and bring me one of their signets as proof of your deeds.","back":"The Al'Aketh cult represents the most direct and urgent danger to our homeland. Their increasingly extremist actions have destabilized our society and damaged our already-weakened connection to the spirits of the four winds. The elements demand action to prove our resilience and resolve, which are traits that are endemic to the domain of the element of earth.","done":"You have returned and brought what I have requested and thus your grit and determination are unquestionable. You are ready for the next step, Harten.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":42.8,"y":23.6,"n":"Windshaper Boro","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"93746":{"id":93746,"t":"A firm response","lv":9,"min":4,"side":"Horde","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Confront Belthaan Brightwish along the road to the Shrine of Akir.\nConfront Belathaan Brightwish","desc":"The High Order has been warned of the consequences of meddling with the Windshaper's affairs. I think we need to make an example out of Belathaan and send him back to the High Order with a few bruises and a healthy respect for the boundaries we set.\nBelathaan was seen leaving town, traveling north towards the Shrine of Akir. I don't know why he was going there, but confronting him alone on the road is the safest option. Find him, and put a bit of fear into his heart.","rew":"You will receive:\nWindshaped Shield 5 Minor Mageblood Elixir\nExperience: 600\n+50 reputation with Windshapers","done":"Wait--what?! Belathaan... is dead?\n<Ayessa listens as you give your account of what occurred.>\nThe High Order was meeting with the Al'Aketh to discuss peace? There is no peace with the cult, they are murderous zealots. What was Elaadrin thinking sending Belathaan to treat with them alone?\nPay this no mind, ‹name›. You are not at fault for this. The arrogance of the High Order is to blame, yet again. You were merely in the right place at the wrong time.","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":59,"y":79.6,"n":"Ayessa Dawnsinger","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"94946":{"id":94946,"t":"The magical city of dalaran","lv":13,"min":7,"side":"Alliance","tag":"new","st":"New in Forever.","obj":"Take the skycutter ship from Zephras Isle to Dalaran City and speak with Danaaris Stargale when you arrive.","desc":"I had intended to be the first of us to step foot onto Azeroth, but recent events with the cult have changed my plans. As a result, I will be remaining here in Valanaar for a time. Fret not though, one of our mages will be waiting to receive you upon your arrival in Dalaran. I'd encourage you to explore Azeroth while we set our affairs in order here. We will call upon you when you are needed.\nWhen you are ready, please proceed to the dock just outside this lodge and board the skycutter ship there.","done":"Ah, you've made it. Wonderful. It's going to take us some time to get ourselves established here, so you may want to take some time to explore the city. Be warned however, try not to venture too far from the safety of the city proper.\nAs idyllic as this new land appears, it can be extremely dangerous to wander outside of Dalaran without appropriate preparation and experience.\nZephras Isle Alterac Mountains","pins":[{"z":"Zephras Isle","x":66.6,"y":79.8,"n":"Elaadrin Evengale","s":1},{"z":"Alterac Mountains","x":12.4,"y":56.2,"n":"Denaaris Stargale","e":1}],"cats":["zephras-isle"]},"8146":{"id":8146,"t":"The Maelstrom's Tendril","lv":60,"min":58,"side":"Both","tag":"changed","st":"Changed in Forever. Requires level 58 instead of 60.","obj":"Maelstrom's Tendril","rew":"You will receive:\nMaelstrom's Tendril\nExperience: 6,600\n+100 reputation with Zandalar Tribe","back":"Even from here I can hear the sound of your volleys laying waste to our enemies. Their cries echo in agony.\nYou have made quite a name for yourself among the trolls of Zandalar, ‹name›. We are grateful for all that you have done.\nHand me your talisman so that I may add another weave.","done":"There is only one more weave that I will be able to add to your talisman, ‹class›","pins":[{"z":"Stranglethorn Vale","x":14.1,"y":13.7,"n":"Falthir the Sightless","e":1,"s":1}],"cats":["zulgurub"]}});